67	Coors Banquet is a pretty good domestic lager	I think it tastes a lot like root beer or cream soda while still being a crisp and refreshing lager. Its delightfully malty and you can really tell that they actually brew it with rocky mountain spring water. I know that sounds like a marketing gimmick but I am from the area where it is brewed and it tastes like the water in my childhood home because it is from a similar source! Being from a mountain does not necessarily mean its good for brewing but the water in that part of Jefferson County actually does work pretty well for making a maltier lager. For its price point its substantially better than alternatives like PBR or Modelo. There's better beer available but there isn't better beer that's quite as cheap except maybe some regional nonsense I haven't tried from far off provinces in the periphery like Michigan or Wisconsin. I don't know that I really believe in that kind of nonsense.\n\nThis isn't really perfectly related but I am currently quite happy with my personal relationship, both platonic and romantic, and that has quite a lot to do with a twitter account thats vaguely coors banquet themed. I think its a little stupid my nickname comes from a beer but its also ok because I don't drink that much but I do like that particular beer so its neither ironic nor a sign of a drinking problem. Twitter is dying as a result of its owner having really bad vibes and its caretakers vibe coding poorly, so I hope this takes off as an alternative to twitter. I think the format is different enough that it may not exactly function as a 1:1 but I also think the format is pretty neat and I'm glad to be able to try it out.\n\n\nI CAN'T BELIEVE I GOT 67	0d962062-5c4f-4fc7-aa4b-a1cafd8bba4f	2025-11-19 06:41:00.419+00	2025-11-19 06:41:54.286+00	f	f	f	\N	f	f
