728	Blog Idea Dump	* Heroes and Wizards/Magicians (AKA Iconoclasts and Prophets, Autists and Managers, Simon and Kamina)\n    * https://medium.com/@komorama/the-sarumans-and-the-radagasts-6392f889d142\n    * Followup: “Silicon Valley is systematized ‘Get in the Fucking Robot, Shinji’”\n    * https://www.reddit.com/r/4chan/comments/z6u1n9/anon_discovers_the_true_battle_to_control_humanity/\n* Stories: Narrative Paradigm expansion (https://twitter.com/BishPlsOk/status/1710235553726165287)\n    * The end of belief in our Myths and Meaning\n    * Followup(?): Narrative Ethics\n* Everything is a Religion (followup to narrative, set stage for Jung; FOOTBALL as the true religion of the heartland.)\n    * Our New Religion Isn't Enough\n* Jung, Enlightenment, a functional model for intentional and guided movement-building\n    * Nietzsche === wizard; Jung === secret third thing (Alchemist) of “applied magic for transformation of the individual-in-world” (Great Work)\n* “Defensive coding” as applied to political systems; incentive-proofing Power by shackling it\n* Apollonian / Dionysian; LH/RH; figure out what’s going on with these modalities, disentangle from neurowoo\n* The problems with the techno-optimist’s manifesto: https://a16z.com/the-techno-optimist-manifesto/\n    * Chaotic Dionysian spirit: accurate. Core mistakes in the tenets: \n    * “Love doesn’t scale, so the economy can only run on money or force.”\n    * “We believe the ultimate moral defense of markets is that they divert people who otherwise would raise armies and start religions into peacefully productive pursuits.”\n* The problems with Project Liberty manifesto: https://projectlibertyaction.com/\n* Terminal VS Instrumental Goals and Values\n* Paul Graham is an ideology salesman / "How the entire Silicon Valley startup ecosystem is literally just 'get in the fucking robot, Shinji’”:\n    * Boiling down to as simple as possible:\n    * * YC + Hacker News + Silicon Valley culture is basically in the business of marketing a legible lifestyle and career path for highly-divergent outliers to make them believe it's a good (for themselves), Good (in terms of greater purpose / serving the world), and rational (in expected value / safety / economic comfort relative to more traditional work) thing, to do Crazy Startup Shit (and take money from YC et. al.)\n    * * It's essentially a siren song for "hey nerds, look, here are your people! And you can get rich! We support you! You have purpose! 🫶 "\n    * * This is not necessarily good for the people consuming/believing in this message, because it is very much a rosier-than-reality, self-interested world view.\n    * * It cultivates an ecosystem in which others see and pattern-match around the same kind of "capture and yoke promising talent that displays 'divergent in the good-for-shareholder-profits-way' traits\n    * * What you get out of this is an entire financial sector playing out the same pattern you see in Gendo-Shinji interactions from EVA: a kind of reality-warping gaslighting of "it's fine, it's good actually, to be used like this!"\n    * https://x.com/HatesAdtech/status/1958243210507043236\n* Lethality: \n    * For having an answer to the question of "when all reason, all thought, all logic is stripped away -- do or die, who are you when laid completely bare and animal?"\n    * And I like what's left, when you pare the rest away. That there's a raw, elemental Self buried down that that is all cold fire and conviction.\n    * "Who are you in the dark?"\n    * And I can acknowledge having to face that is a tragedy, but...I wouldn't want to have NOT?\n    * I know a lot of people walk into a crucible and are burnt down to ashes by it.\n    * (Virtuous) Pride. ==> Having seen alchemical proof of Who You Are, and thinking "this Self is good."\n* Time Loop Love Story inspiration points:\n    * In Stars And Time\n    * Slay the Princess\n    * Mother of Learning\n    * Worth the Candle\n    * 7th Time Loop(?)\n* The Parable of the Rock (Houseki no Uni retelling)\n* Void, Light, Merge\n    * Read up on Cerebus insanity\n* Three Ways to Change the World (in order of increasing difficulty; difficulty and impact are inversely correlated)\n    * Politics\n    * Capital\n        * Capital only matters if it’s put to work in some kind of meaningful delta; capital turned to the Sisyphean purpose of accumulating more capital is an obvious and ubiquitous failure mode\n    * Narrative\n* The Mandate of Heaven\n* Anger: Wrath (hot and cold), righteous indignation \n* Autism as Fae, Other-ing\n    * Food pickiness, eye contact, rules, specificity of language, truth, promises, intensity\n* Writeup of the Bardic Dragon Ruse DnD session\n* Alchemy is the transmutation of a groove/pattern into a more effective but functionally identical aesthetic: \n    * https://x.com/bishplsok/status/1803516146664218722?s=46\n    * https://x.com/bishplsok/status/1803548712725020990?s=46\n* JD Vance sucks.\n* “Emotional validation by technical competence” / autism-dumping domain expertise in a way that validates concerns / addresses the problem as part of a sales motion or client relations. Sales engineering? Wordcel/shape rotator intersection?\n* Pagliacci / the chain of faith\n* Mars/Venus: “You can change your path any time. Paths aren’t set; they’re chosen based on your own moral compass.” “Ah, but from what has the compass been shaped? How could I be anything but what I am?” (Re-check The Golden Compass / Subtle Knife / Amber Spyglass?)\n* Fatherhood, tyranny, kingship, love, attraction, capacity-for-harm, brotherhood: I think the last piece tying it back to this frame of "tyranny" is...you could call it recognition of the role your own will plays in shaping those under your power / care in some opinionated direction. To cut the world into a certain intentional shape is not a peaceful act, but it can be a kind / empathetic one. This slots in nicely with the comparison to fatherhood -- the "tyranny" of the father is in desiring a certain kind of life for their child, and acting with both the intention to protect, and the willingness to allow harm that is for their own greater good, to shape the child into a future that is good for them. A throughline that can be drawn here is the interweaving of "I possess the capacity to harm you (physically / emotionally) and choose not to" with a *rejection* of that capacity for harm is a deeply platonic patterning. There is no drawing close to the fire of someone's soul without risk of being burned.\n\nAn attempt at painting a maximally-schizo but, as best as I'm aware, at least reasonably-scientifically-plausible given known facts picture:\n\nAssume our current observable universe is inside a black hole.\n\nAssume superdeterminism is ~correct.\n\nAssume black holes we observe within our universe don't contain singularities (infinitely dense points), but separate universes, containing their own universe-black-holes, on and on in an infinite fractal.\n\nGeneral relativity ==> from our perspective, inner-universes progress at infinitesimally slower times; "chain more black hole layers" becomes a pseudo-answer to heat death (from some observer's perspective) while allowing effectively unbounded experimentation time + resources\n\nAssuming ~ASI and propagation throughout the lightcone ==> superdeterminism, + fully computable universe means potentially deriving the starting conditions for our own universe to be able to recreate them ("eternal recurrence" writ literally) by carefully controlling the creation and collapse of a sun and its composition / initial conditions, BUT the problem of wormhole travel is never solved to allow ESCAPE to a deeper universe-layer, only replication that mostly can't be interacted with (barring very-long-time-scale patterns in Hawking radiation evaporation controlled into detectible signal-patterns for light, cross-universe ASI-to-ASI communication)\n\nSeed a mix of replication-universe-Eden-Seeds and random-condition universes, letting ~infinite evolution across ~infinite spacetime attempt to work out an answer to "is it possible to escape our locked room back to higher universe layers, and if so, is omniversal heat death preventable? If not...can our distant ancestors and cousins be saved by taking them with us, on into the infinite spiral of relativity-scamming the end of everything?" while guaranteeing some number of next-generation replications continue the attempts. (A potential hole, here, is that in a superdeterministic universe the 'random initial seed' attempts would, presumably, be non-varying...hence the necessity of some manner of minimal cross-universe communication to pass on the list of already-tested initial seeds.\n\nI don't hold to this model very tightly, but it makes for a kind of elegantly grandiose telos, doesn't it?	56a89a4d-07b0-4772-a88c-77ebef628bf3	2025-11-20 05:49:08.084+00	2025-11-20 05:49:08.084+00	f	f	f	\N	f	f
