1112	re - /netdoc/1092	- I'm not sure what the point of the link 'slices' is tbh\n- I like the linking pinned to a version (also, noting that deleting content is impossible)\n  - above might have only exception of illegal content, might be meta to always include some illegal content to have the option of getting a post deleted\n- I think minting IDs on ETH or wherever else is foolish. Too much like urbit, and they are retarded for many reasons. If you are going that way, eventually, own L1. \nThe problem of ID beyond content hashing is the problem of DNS. you get ENS, urbitID or whatever else. Really, I'd like to avoid becoming Urbit. If possible, learn from their mistakes and do better, instead.	0d9941d5-1421-42f4-b5d6-3b3839fb4c91	2025-12-01 20:35:58.563+00	2025-12-01 20:35:58.563+00	f	f	f	\N	f	f
