4v	tone	as a general rule, the actual words you say are less powerful than the tone you speak them in. this is because words are oft wasted, and therefore have lost some prominence. when words mean nothing, you need context to solve them: body language, facial expressions, others' reactions to it. conversations are easy if you remember words don't really matter.\n\nthe problem arises when, every so often, you encounter someone who reminds you words really do matter. more than most things, in fact. they hold up a mirror to you, and you notice a mirror is all you've ever been. when words mean nothing, you forget how to say what you mean.\n\nwhen i was a little girl, i thought i said all the wrong things. i thought it would be simpler to never speak at all. when i was a bigger girl, i read a book about a teenager with selective mutism, and i thought she was the coolest character ever invented. i wanted to be just like her. but i was all full of words, and i couldn't shut up for long. with time, i learned i was just saying them in the wrong way, and i adjusted my tone accordingly. people will forgive what you say as long as they can tell you meant well. correction, though, easily slips into overcorrection. people close to me, people who knew me before i grew terrified of speaking, are often frustrated. Do You Take Anything Seriously? they now ask. Do You Have Any Genuine Thoughts, Any Sincerity Left, Or Are You Just A Joke Machine? my well of words has run dry, and all i have left to say is I Don't Know What To Say.\n\ncall me speechless, call me crazy, call me an undersocialized late bloomer. (just don't call me late to dinner, please.)\n\ntone became a conversational crutch for me, i suppose. and it worked really well, so well i forgot how powerful bare words are. soon enough i will need to learn how to speak again. i will learn to say what i mean and mean what i say. i will stop being so afraid of words, one day. and maybe one day tone will be only a background to the conversation, not the bulk of it, one day.	fe0e2bca-802b-45d8-8713-b5d7bbb8b7fd	2026-01-20 23:05:42.668643+00	2026-01-20 23:05:42.668643+00	f	f	f	\N	f	f
