3d	Investor Contract Draft	# DRAFT – NON-BINDING\n# THIS DRAFT IS FOR DISCUSSION PURPOSES ONLY AND DOES NOT CONSTITUTE A BINDING AGREEMENT.\n# NO PARTY SHALL HAVE ANY OBLIGATION UNLESS AND UNTIL A DEFINITIVE AGREEMENT IS EXECUTED BY ALL PARTIES.\n# Investment Agreement (Draft)\n\nThis agreement is between Netaris LLC, a Wyoming limited liability company (the “Company”), represented by Diego Cabello and Gregory Mockler, and ______________________ (the “Investor”).\n\n## 1. Valuation and Units\n\nThe Company is valued at $400,000 on a pre-money, fully diluted basis.\n\nThe Company has authorized 4,000 membership units (the “Units”), each with a price of $100 per Unit.\n\nImmediately prior to this investment, the Company is owned 50% by Diego Cabello and 50% by Greg Mockler, holding all issued Units.\n\nThis agreement represents the first issuance of Units to a non-founder.\n\n## 2. Investment Structure\n\nThe Investor may acquire up to 600 Units for an aggregate purchase price of $60,000, as follows:\n\na. Initial Tranche  \nUpon execution of a definitive agreement, the Investor shall pay $10,000 and receive 100 Units.\n\nb. Subsequent Tranches  \nThe Investor may make subsequent payments of $5,000 per tranche, with each such payment entitling the Investor to 50 Units, until either:\n\n*   600 Units have been issued, or\n*   $60,000 has been paid in total.\n\nPayments after the initial tranche shall commence on May 1, 2026, and occur monthly thereafter, subject to a two (2) week grace period.\n\n## 3. Issuance of Units\n\nUnits shall be issued only upon receipt by the Company of the corresponding payment for each tranche.\n\nNo Units are issued, vested, or owed with respect to any unpaid or incomplete tranche.\n\n## 4. Missed Payments and Forfeiture\n\nIf the Investor fails to make any tranche payment within the applicable two-week grace period:\n\na. No further Units shall be issued to the Investor;  \nb. The Investor shall permanently forfeit the right to acquire any future tranches under this agreement;  \nc. The Investor shall retain only those Units actually issued and paid for prior to default.\n\nAny Units not issued as a result of such forfeiture shall remain authorized but unissued and may be issued by the Company in its sole discretion.\n\n## 5. Voting Rights\n\nThe Investor shall have voting rights strictly proportional to the number of Units actually issued and outstanding in the Investor’s name, as provided under the Company’s Operating Agreement.\n\n## 6. No Additional Rights\n\nExcept as expressly set forth herein, the Investor receives rights not including management rights, board rights and control rights.\n\n## 7. Transfer Restrictions\n\nThe Investor may not sell, assign, pledge, or otherwise transfer any Units without the prior written consent of the Company, except as permitted under the Operating Agreement or applicable law.\n\n## 8. Securities Law Acknowledgment\n\nThe Investor acknowledges that the Units are being issued in a private transaction exempt from registration under applicable securities laws and are being acquired for investment purposes only, and not with a view to resale.\n\n## 9. Governing Law and Venue\n\nThis agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Wyoming, without regard to conflict-of-laws principles.\n\nThe parties consent to exclusive jurisdiction and venue in the state and federal courts located in Wyoming and waive any objection thereto.\n\n## 10. Entire Agreement\n\nThis agreement constitutes the entire understanding between the parties with respect to the subject matter hereof and supersedes all prior discussions, messages, or understandings, whether written or oral.\n\n## 11. Amendments\n\nThis agreement may be amended only by a written instrument executed by both the Company and the Investor.\n\n## 12. Severability\n\nIf any provision of this agreement is held to be invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions shall remain in full force and effect.\n\n## 13. Assignment\n\nThe Investor may not assign this agreement without the prior written consent of the Company. The Company may assign this agreement in connection with a merger, reorganization, or sale of substantially all assets.\n\n## 14. Counterparts and Electronic Signatures\n\nThis agreement may be executed in counterparts, including via electronic signature, each of which shall be deemed an original.\n\n## Signature Blocks\n\n- (placeholder)	ca82df4d-b69e-4506-89bb-f86531d07d81	2026-01-14 03:49:19.314273+00	2026-01-14 03:49:19.314273+00	t	f	f	\N	f	f
