4g	hamilton	good morning netaris. today is going to be a good day \n\ni have smoked a cig multiple times today, have had a coffee, and did not sleep on the train last night. \n\nnetaris is still a small platform, so this is for a small audience right now. i am very excited about this platform becoming a system that will interact with many aspects of its users' daily life. of course, this entails expansion from merely a platform. it also entails much reading and research from my part. \n\ni will be documenting the growth of this system, partially on this account, partially under various pseudonyms. some accounts with [stylometric obfuscation](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adversarial_stylometry), and some without. it will be fairly easy to tell which ones *without* obfuscation are by me. at the age of 21, i think i have a fairly distinct style, especially considering the even less broadly-distributed corpus i wrote in the last couple years. go ahead and visit [diegocabello.com](https://diegocabello.com) to take a look at some of that. that website, by the way, is a progenitor to many ideas i am putting into this platform. for the intentionally obfuscated accounts i intend to not use computer tools for obfuscation, as an exercise. \n\nalexander hamilton wrote some of the federalist papers with a distinct style, anonymously, and some of them were attributed to him by stylometric methods in the 70s using the unix tool grep ([see](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NTfOnGZUZDk)). and unix was never perfect, and i don't believe that these systems that i am designing now will be looked at as perfect in over half a century from now. (i do, however, believe that they will be *looked at*). the systems alexander hamilton designed for the united states are not perfect, but we use some of them, and they still work. like hamilton, i cannot claim being born to two united states-born parents (no points for guessing where my family name is from). but, like hamilton, i love america.	ca82df4d-b69e-4506-89bb-f86531d07d81	2026-01-18 15:18:08.760012+00	2026-01-18 18:33:06.131+00	f	f	f	\N	f	f
