5c	scrap	the proof is that you need two encoders, a delimiter one-of-one and unique, and then any symbol encoder. binary is irreducible, so this representation would have to be built on top of binary. the shortest sequence (a sequence is >1) that you can have that is *distinguishable* from any other sequence is two bits. two bits leaves us with one as a delimiter, and three others as symbol encoders. we choose 11 as the delimiter, and 00, 01, and 10 as the encoders. the preferred way is balanced ternary (-1, 0, 1) represented over binary and delimited by quaternary\n\nthe proof is that you need two encoders, a delimiter one-of-one and unique, and then any symbol encoder. binary is irreducible, so this representation would have to be built on top of binary. the shortest sequence (a sequence is >1) that you can have that is *distinguishable* from any other sequence is two bits. two bits leaves us with one as a delimiter, and three others as symbol encoders. we choose 11 as the delimiter, and 00, 01, and 10 as the encoders. the preferred way is balanced ternary (-1, 0, 1) represented over binary and delimited by quaternary	ca82df4d-b69e-4506-89bb-f86531d07d81	2026-01-23 13:42:40.955333+00	2026-01-23 13:44:02.683+00	f	f	f	\N	f	f
