309	517	• Ortho-K •\n\nThe blackout curtains felt quite grey,\nWhich struck my empty eye,\nAs low light (love) had blurred your face\nWhen you last kissed me bye.\n\nThen laying, Luna let me off,\nBypassing bark and bite,\nWas sated by mistaken thought,\nWe’d reconvene next night.\n\nAnd frightened, the surrounding cars\nBegged blinded wheels to flight.\nMy lens confused the shining stars \nWith yellow traffic light.\n\nRegretful, foolish, wanton trade\nOf safety, sight, and sin,\nBut left contacts if left unpaid,\nI’d chance my life again.\n\n\n\n• (to be titled) •\n\n2013 Wattpad fiction wormed its way into my brain.\nI didn't trust the blue D.A.R.E men who told me be afraid.\nSo huddled, hiding, under covers, I peeked in Sapphire's place.\nAnd the fear/freedom of progressive love peaked inside my veins.\n\nBut user once and junky twice, I caught the red faced bug.\nThe dripping need throughout the week to get a hit of smut.\nUnrefined, cut with fetish tags, I scarfed down literotica.\nAnd the drops of lust held on my spoon never were enough.\n\n\n\n\n\n• Makes 2 servings •\n\nWhen my parents pressed pause \non Spongebob’s high cost,\nI simply settled for Ming,\nAnd that Child hood swing\nwas lost Heart and Soul in Cook’s Country.\n\nAnd the evenings alone\nSurrounding the stove,\nI blasted Babish on loop,\nSipping Saffitz sweet soup\nIn the stillness of undergrad air.\n\nThen you\nEntered my kitchen\nAnd showed me what food was about.\nMy eyes starved of the plate.\nDishes float in their way.\nAnd dinner was always for you.\n\nBut the evenings alone\nSurrounding the stove,\nWhen tears sped up to a run,\nI chopped onions for one\nFor a recipe meant to serve 2.\n\n\n\n• beg you never •\n\nHands quaking.\nBreath taken thinking 'bout the\nPhone call home,\nAlone,\nTo a wrong number.\n\nPlans escape my plan.\nGod you’ll know what happened\nTo us.\nSo much,\nPray, love, and beg you never\n\nHate me, and break me, and kick me, and put me under,\nFake ease round, take me down (just please I want to see you),\nSlap me, and shoot me, and treat me just like your garbage,\nShake me off, pay me not, just please, I want to see you now.\n\nCall your number.\nIs it any wonder?\nI’ll know that I’m right, but\nI’ll start to think it’s my blunder.\n\nHows the weather?\nWill this last forever?\nOne day we’ll get by, but\nI’ll have to beg that you never\n	2025-12-23 19:58:14.414+00	Poems and Songs	ce785309-d263-4cbe-ab9d-0950b3551d50
