area who were really committed to it could have dug some cables underground and connected to eachother on it. this might be happening in some places, but we just wouldn't know about it because we are not on that network.\n\nor even scarier still, there could be a few people who are telepathic in the head and have all connected to eachother, and are operating as a hive mind. if this is the case right now, then the number of people in the hiveminds must be very small. anything more than, like, 5 people would be noticeable. there is just no possible way to obscure that.\n\nor even *worse*, a small group of people could have figured out how to clip out of physical reality entirely and hopped aboard an alien spaceship and moved to a completely different plane entirely. heaven's gate tried it. but if that ever really works it would probably be by a rogue group of mad scientists (like the ones who made covid).\n\nyou know those shots in *serial experiments lain*, where there are a bunch of wires on the poles, and there is a loud droning buzz? whoever wrote that show knew what was going on. at the ending (spoilers are okay on netaris) when lain was in a world that overlapped but did not intersect with the real world, in the world of "the wired"...\n\nbasically, the wires that span the world form a *substrate* that all the human organisms get online to. damn "the power of communication". damn "a super-intelligent organism". damn "the power of human ingenuity". you are on the internet now. we are doing something strange. we are building something that we don't quite know what part we play in, all of us. you are part of the *superstrate*.\n\nwelcome to the internet. the old internet, the new internet, whatever. you're reading this via HTTP, nerd. how long have you been online? how long has your longest internet break lasted you? i doubt very long. i doubt internet is healthy for a child's development, but from when you are a teenager till at least 40, you are stuck on the inte