103	1038	Here are the netaris style guides. \n\n- no perpendicular lines should touch unless it is to indicate a major division of content. for example, there shouldn't be any perpendicular contact in the dividing line between the tabbar and the urlbar because those two things are part of the "top" division. having extra division there draws the eye in too many different places. we need to have a consistent design language\n- the bold yellow should be tried to use as sparsely as possible, and only to communicate major divisions. see how gray is used for the urlbar and the horizontal dividers for the sidebar footer and above the postform \n- i want the user experience for this to be "a browser within a browser". as little as possible should we use built-in browser functionality like built-in popups or notifications.	2025-11-28 04:40:17.184+00	stylistic	ca82df4d-b69e-4506-89bb-f86531d07d81
