95	1031	To the beginner mathematician, mathematics is quite easy to define. But as the numbers get more lettered, and the letters get more greek, this is no longer the case. At some point, quotients get formed by putting one number over another but by invoking the lattice isomorphism theorem. When the identity automorphism becomes trivial to define, the identity of math as a subject is not.\n\nFor most subjects there is an intention or physical body anchoring and driving the area forwards. Biology is about living things. Psychology is about cognition. Civil engineering is about structures. But mathematics does not have this one (or two) word encapsulation. There is no “thing” that math is about. Computational Algebra looks nothing like analytic number theory. I can barely hold a conversation with my friends who are studying partial differential equations, even though I am technically one toe in the field of differential geometry.	2025-11-26 18:30:06.5+00	Defining Math	ce785309-d263-4cbe-ab9d-0950b3551d50
