180	1092	new one. topics are transclusion and bidirectional linking; and purpose-built browser and mobile app.\n\nyesterday i realized that having the protolink/neolink configuration is super helpful for checking embed versioning. i think the protolinks are gonna have to be a tuple of the doc uri and the version hash. separately, there should be a separate field for the "parent" one. chat/comment functionality is too common to get rid of that or do some fucky thing to combine "parent" and "paleolinks" and try and make it elegant. there is the slight consideration of "do we want a document to have more than one parent". but implementing one parent, protolinks, and neolinks shouldn't be too challenging to implement with what we already have. \n\nfor transclusion, i think we should do something like python-style slices. in the embed, it would look something like \n\n`netdot/2323[234:904]`\n\nwhere the numbers inside are the character positions. i can't think of anything better. \n\nshould also probably have something for when someone wants to include the beginning of a document. like `netdoc/2323/[:904]` to show the first few sentences. i am opposed to doing the tail, because that *could* lead to abuse. maybe if you were a huge fan of shakespearean couplets or something. \n\nand then when you do a transclusion, it would update the protolinks and neolinks fields for those specific documents. \n\ni started doing browser stuff. pretty cool. going to package the electron app as the browser, people *can* use it as an editor for things to conform to the schema locally and then upload stuff to the network. would use the `better-sqlite3` npm package. \n\nwe also need to define what you can do with and without an account. i think *viewing* public docs is a good idea, but not any other actions. the browser should allow some offline functionality for not being logged in, like creating, updating, and retrieving, but *not* pushing to a server. \n\nalso, i want to make a react-native app that (for now) doesn't have any functionality besides doing push notifications. i want netaris to become my default messaging app soon, and if i am out and around i am not checking my safari browser and no one lets websites do push notifications. \n\nfolder grouping also needs to be a thing. (a folder is a netdoc with a title, a blank content field, and neolinks being the child documents?) if we can figure out how to get that down (and if we add voip), that is our discord killer. 	2025-12-01 01:22:43.032+00	sunday	ca82df4d-b69e-4506-89bb-f86531d07d81
