ns\n\n- the folder icon should have a plus on it because it is make a new folder \n- same thing with the new netdoc icon \n- upload icon (download icon upside down staple shaped thing at the top). would go with sidebar icons\n- right now i had claude/gemini make all the icons. they look good, but they could all be made *slightly* more consistent with eachother. like with stroke width\n- (also color) the icon button outlines probably shouldn't use the main yellow like they do now \n- needs to be something for all the edit icons (edit/cancel, cache, save) to be stuck together. right now the button component has a fixed-outline, but i \nwould like there to be something where the three icons are in one rounded rectangle with borders seperating them, and maybe they collapse "save" and "cache" if you are not in edit mode. \n- need stylistically consistent icons for the sidebar footer\n\n### pages/components\n\n- the titles for the pages (new netdoc, the other ones) need to be stylistically consistent\n- make the yellow horizontal rules in settings and profile gray instead of yellow \n- the dms header needs to be bigger and it needs a horizontal rule\n- perhaps document embeds for the author could inherit the author's color. have tried it and i think it would look good in some contexts but not others\n- document embeds right now have the darker yellow outline, which violates the design language right now. embeds aren't like big parts of the ui\n- netdoc header status indicator needs to change to a different yellow\n- the permissions admin page needs to be completely redone and made stylistically consistent with everything else\n- for the icon toolbar, it would be *really* cool if where you were hovering over the icon, the tooltip shows up in the exact same spot and doesn't move around (so you can actually read it), but there are two lines going from your cursor to the tooltip rectangle filling in a triangle (so you can see where your cursor is while reading it). \n- perpendicular lines for uploading media need to be changed\n- need to make a "customize toolbar" widget in the settings tab. there are a lot of buttons in the netdoc header, and some people might not want all of them to be there. some of them *need* to be there, and some of them do not. as a list they are\n    - required: edit, save, share, permissions, subscribe\n    - not required: history, cache, make available offline (netbrowser only, not implemented yet) \n\n### theme\n\n- right now the concept is "old yellow crt sulfur terminal". this is not something i want to deviate from. it is pretty close, but what would be *really* cool is if if like you could see the pixel lines like you would with an old terminal like that, and if there was a slight (1px, and not consistent, a partial outline) flickering glow around everything. it's good because technical (or just initiated) people get it when they see it, but non-technical people don't feel like they *don't* get it when they see it.\n- i think having a few featured official themes is a good idea, but getting the first theme down is the most important. but making other themes would be good for honing getting the main theme down right\n- we *could* support user-made custom themes, but really again i think we also need to worry about saving the user from their own bad taste\n\n### other \n\n- font rendering: i think the default font weight needs to be a little thinner, and bold needs to be heavier. right now it is hard to tell them apart. this should be a simple fix\n- wordmark: we need a really good wordmark. i want to use custom font, custom design, not take a font from dafont.com, i don't want to use ai, not even for concept art. need a human \n- monospaced concept: this might be kind of difficult, but if *everything* could align to the same grid as the font, that would be really cool (using css grid). it would make making a TUI much easier. different font sizes for headers kind of mess this up, but it *could* still work (make everything take up two character heights and then inside that change the size as needed)\neditor: to be an obsidian killer, the build-in editor needs to be pretty good. i would like headings to render big, italics and bold to render with their underscores/asterixes (sic), and links to render with a different color and underlined even while you are editing it. \n- editor: to be an obsidian killer, the build-in editor needs to be pretty good. i would like headings to render big, italics and bold to render with their underscores/asterixes (sic), and links to render with a different color and underlined even while you are editing it. 	2025-12-01 20:21:55.019+00	stylistic 2	ca82df4d-b69e-4506-89bb-f86531d07d81
167	1048	# features to add\n\n- [ ] live multiplayer editing (use CDRT postgres extension?)\n    - would also be cool to have live cursors\n- [ ] graph view!!! \n    - [X] make space for it in new tab \n- [ ] document ids should be b32\n\n# security\n\n- [X] json schema validation for settings post route\n- [ ] all the pen testing screenshots from wednesday nov 26th\n\n# bugs \n\n- title bugs\n    - [ ] when you update netdoc title, it doesn't update in sidebar\n    - [ ] versions should show titles\n    - [X] updating the title makes the editor collapse unexpectedly \n- [ ] notifications are kind of broken \n- [X] add a "cancel" button next to "save"\n- [X] markdown rendering seems to be fucked in mobile safari\n- [X] editing (both editor and message bar) should persist state if you click out of the tab\n    - [X] new netdoc, netdoc header\n    - [X] postform\n- [ ] underscores seem to be breaking for profile links\n- [X] implement a stylistically-consistent pop-up window (this one isn't that important)\n- [X] should say "does not exist" when it doesn't exist but right now it says "restricted"\n- [X] joined date\n- [X] old versions shouldn't give you a "cannot access"\n- [X] links update in orthobrowser bar and correct tab selection saves state if you click out of orthobrowser tab\n- [3/4] implement toggle bar functionality for\n    - [X] adult splash texts\n    - [X] open in same/tab vs. open in new tab preference (sidebar, embed, feed) -- might need viewer\n    - [X] misspelling red line indicator on vs. off preference\n    - [1/2] show by default the "lose unsaved content" popup window\n- [X] the above point will require:\n    - a short json string stored in postgres. whenever the user loads the page again in a new tab it pulls the json with their profile and if they change a setting it posts the changes to postgres and gets a response containing the exact same thing - so the changes don't take effect locally if they don't push. and whenever the page loads, it uses the locally stored json\n    - it's not optimistic loading. if the user changes it live, then i guess the changes persist. but if the user does a close and reopen the tab, deleting local storage, then the source of truth is postgres\n    - the postgres storage for the profile is *server* handling and is NOT part of the profile primitive when we give that out eventually\n- [X] markdown rendering needs to be changed in some places\n    - there needs to be limited markdown rendering for blockquotes and headers in comments. this would happen in netdocviewer\n    - bullet points and numbered lists look fucky when you send it in your own messages\n- [X] dms top bar is in fact not fixed\n- [X] need to be able to delete media from the post form after you upload it and before you send it\n\n## stylistic stuff\n\n- [X] unsubscribe button has double border in expanded view\n- [ ] there are vertical perpendicular bars on the media upload and on the new tab button, and in postform media upload\n\n---\n\n\nhere is the link to the last one /netdoc/427	2025-11-30 04:32:15.708+00	bugs 2	ca82df4d-b69e-4506-89bb-f86531d07d81
