172	1092	new one. we are gonna write about transclusion and bidirectional linking. \n\nyesterday i realized that having the protolink/neolink configuration is super helpful for checking embed versioning. i think the protolinks are gonna have to be a tuple of the doc uri and the version hash. separately, there should be a separate field for the "parent" one. chat/comment functionality is too common to get rid of that or do some fucky thing to try and make it elegant. implementing that shouldn't be too challenging to implement with what we already have. \n\nfor transclusion, i think we should do something like python-style slices. in the embed, it would look something like \n\n`/netdoc/2323[234:504]`\n\nwhere the numbers inside are the character positions. i can't think of anything better. \n\nand then when you do a transclusion, it would update the protolinks and neolinks fields for those specific documents. 	2025-12-01 01:05:47.797+00	sunday	ca82df4d-b69e-4506-89bb-f86531d07d81
