now the copy link functionality breaks it\n- favicon: for the life of me i cannot figure out where the favicon is supposed to go. i've tried everywhere but it still renders the default vite icon. \n- sounds: probably a notification and ringtone sound. worth starting to think about now, but we should probably find a really good sound designer when we have more sounds we need than just two	2025-12-01 21:04:19.742+00	stylistic 2	ca82df4d-b69e-4506-89bb-f86531d07d81
176	1092	new one. we are gonna write about transclusion and bidirectional linking. \n\nyesterday i realized that having the protolink/neolink configuration is super helpful for checking embed versioning. i think the protolinks are gonna have to be a tuple of the doc uri and the version hash. separately, there should be a separate field for the "parent" one. chat/comment functionality is too common to get rid of that or do some fucky thing to try and make it elegant. implementing that shouldn't be too challenging to implement with what we already have. \n\nfor transclusion, i think we should do something like python-style slices. in the embed, it would look something like \n\n`netdot/2323[234:904]`\n\nwhere the numbers inside are the character positions. i can't think of anything better. \n\nshould also probably have something for when someone wants to include the beginning of a document. like \n\n`netdoc/2323/[:904]` \n\nto show the first few sentences. i am opposed to doing the tail, because that *could* lead to abuse. maybe if you were a huge fan of shakespearean couplets or something. \n\nand then when you do a transclusion, it would update the protolinks and neolinks fields for those specific documents. 	2025-12-01 01:09:33.363+00	sunday	ca82df4d-b69e-4506-89bb-f86531d07d81
