332	2h	i have been finding some odd lexical gaps while making this app. i am going to plug a few of them here. \n\n- *delimiter*\n    - a prefix of one or more characters that denotes what something is\n    - from [wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delimiter) : "In computing, a delimiter is a character or a sequence of characters for specifying the boundary between separate, independent regions in data such as a text file or data stream."\n    - this is an already filled lexical gap\n- *delineator* \n    - a single-character delimiter. examples include `@` \n- *cartouche*\n    - a delimiter in an http path segment delimited by a preceding and succeeding slash `/`. 	2026-01-12 21:18:47.683+00	Terminology	ca82df4d-b69e-4506-89bb-f86531d07d81
