311	1115	also for minari\n\n# marketing \n\n- social media campaign on twitter\n- hype posting\n\n# landing page and onboarding\n\n- you should be able to view documents, browse the network, and draft a document without an account, but be unable to publish anything or send a message\n- there is a *tiny* bit of learning to do to use this network, which is mostly how to use the "everything is a netdoc" philosophy (really, everything is one of two primitives and the derived interactions between those two, a netdoc and a netid, but we haven't figured out the netid part yet so we won't tell them that right now)\n- we should definitely make an "upload obsidian vault", "transfer discord server", "transfer notion", and "import google drive/onedrive" one-and-done functionality. platform killers right there\n\n# launch\n\n- invite codes? \n- staging\n    - a couple weeks ago we did our launch to beta testers and they found all sorts of stuff wrong with the app, but they really liked it\n    - we need to move the discord server to netaris itself once the app is reliable enough and a few features have been added like voice chat and better managed group permissions and folders-as-documents\n    - i am thinking we do a second beta launch, where we basically tell our beta testers "hey we added all these cool new features and fixed these bugs and the app is good enough to stand on its own, come migrate here" - but we don't push that as our *big* launch. we let word of mouth kind of simmer before we push our big launch\n\n# target audiences\n\n- everybody (the whole internet)\n- power users\n- kill list\n    - obsidian\n    - discord\n    - notion\n    - google docs\n    - twitter (sad) \n\n	2026-01-12 05:48:04.855+00	user acquisition	ca82df4d-b69e-4506-89bb-f86531d07d81
