336	2h	i have been finding some odd lexical gaps while making this app. i am going to plug a few of them here. \n\n- *delimiter*\n    - a sequence of one or more characters that separates two pieces of data\n    - this is an already filled lexical gap. see [wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delimiter) \n- *delineator* \n    - a single-character delimiter\n    - the most commonly used is `@`, and the only other main one is cashapp which uses `$`\n    - from the latin word *delineare* which means "to draw a line"\n    - this is not a previously filled lexical gap\n- *cartouche*\n    - a delimiter in an http path segment delimited by a preceding and succeeding slash `/`. 	2026-01-12 21:25:27.466+00	Terminology	ca82df4d-b69e-4506-89bb-f86531d07d81
