p which uses `$`, reddit which uses `u/` (note the slash delineator), and urbit which uses `~`.\n- *extension*\n    - another common one. this is a file extension that comes at the end of a file name, such as `.txt`.\n\n\nhere is what this taxonomy looks like in an ASCII tree:\n\n```\n                    DETERMINATIVE\n                      /        \\\n                     /          \\\n                    /            \\\n             SEPARATOR          MARKER\n                 |               /    \\\n             DELIMITER          /      \\\n                 |             /        \\\n            DELINEATOR      SIGIL    EXTENSION\n```\n\n\nfrom this, we can make one more interesting construction worth pointing out. \n\n- *cartouche*\n    - a cartouche is a sequence of a leading slash delineator `/`, a delimiter, and a following slash delineator `/`. term used to describe reoccurring file paths or http path segments (such as api routes).\n    - this is the contemporary egyptology term to describe a container enclosing text. it comes from the french word for "cartridge" which napoleon's army used to describe these symbols when they were in egypt. 	2026-01-21 01:55:55.996+00	Determinatives	ca82df4d-b69e-4506-89bb-f86531d07d81
