615	1173	I landed in Philadelphia at 8 am. By 11 am, we had gotten acquainted, seen the unfortunately boring liberty bell, and had made plans to walk to my friend's coffee shop. The stroll was made a trek by the heat, humidity (an eastern feature you were not accustomed to), and assortments of bags we needed to lug around. By the time we arrived at the cafe you were gassed. We rested for a little and got pointed towards a restaraunt where I could get a banh mi at. This was fortunately pretty close by. While I was eating you were able to recuperate from the compounded effects of the climate, your lack of sleep, and what was probably the aftereffects of your somewhat recent surgery. The conversation picked back up as we sat in the air conditioned shade of the hipster vietnamese shop, and you resumed telling me about the lore of the assassin's creed games you had just marathoned. I asked if you wanted to see the river and you confessed that you were much too exhausted to do so. Thirty minutes and five triple a plots explained later, we got into an uber and riffed all the way back to the airport, where our bus was to pick us up from. The only one we have documented is "disappointed leg fetishist seeing a picture of a foot be like its alright but it needs motion." \n\nWe joined the crowd of campers awaiting the bus. At first we waited inside but as the time approached for the buses to arrive, the group slowly shuffled out the door. It was now properly hot too. Philly reached 90F and the humidity made it feel like 100F. I was dressed for the weather. You were not. After thirty minutes stood sweltering, the buses arrived and we got on board. We took the front seats in hope that it would be the coolest part of the bus. 	2026-01-23 22:04:52.52+00	VC Day 1	ce785309-d263-4cbe-ab9d-0950b3551d50
