673	5t	# commands\n\n- here "kind of" means "the server implements it differently"\n    - `/kick` is available to owner only, and takes netaris username not irc nickname \n    - see section header FLAGS for `/mode`\n    - `/nick` is not callable from the text box. instead, display name is set in netaris settings\n\n| Command  | What it does                       | Who can use it                                 |     Implemented?      | \n| -------- | ---------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | :-------------------: | \n| SQUIT    | Disconnect a server link           | Operators                                      |          no           |\n| REHASH   | Reload server config               | Operators                                      |          no           | \n| WALLOPS  | Message to all operators           | Operators                                      |          no           |\n| OPERWALL | Alias for WALLOPS                  | Operators                                      |          no           |\n| RESTART  | Restart server                     | Operators                                      |          no           |\n| KILL     | Forcibly disconnect a user         | Operators                                      |          no           |\n| CONNECT  | Tell server to connect to another  | Operators                                      |          no           |\n| PASS     | Send password before registration  | On connect                                     |          no           | \n| USER     | Set username/realname on connect   | On connect                                     |          no           |\n| SERVER   | Server-to-server link registration | Servers only                                   |          no           |\n| OPER     | Authenticate as IRC operator       | With credentials                               |          no           |\n| PING     | Keepalive request                  | Usually server-initiated                       |          no           |\n| PONG     | Keepalive response                 |                                                |          no           |\n| TRACE    | Trace route to server              | Limited; Operators (full)                      |          no           |\n| LINKS    | List linked servers                |                                                |          no           |\n| ERROR    | Server error message               | Servers only                                   |          no           |\n| USERS    | List users on server host          | If enabled                                     |          no           |\n| AWAY     | Set away message                   |                                                |          no           |\n| USERHOST | Quick user host lookup             |                                                |          no           |\n| PRIVMSG  | Send message to user/channel       |                                                |          no           |\n| NOTICE   | Like PRIVMSG but no auto-reply     |                                                |          no           |\n| MODE     | Set user or channel modes          | Self (user modes), Channel ops (channel modes) |        kind of        |\n| NICK     | Set or change nickname             |                                                |        kind of        |\n| QUIT     | Disconnect from server             |                                                |        kind of        |\n| JOIN     | Join a channel                     |                                                |        kind of        |\n| PART     | Leave a channel                    |                                                |        kind of        |\n| KICK     | Kick user from channel             | Channel ops                                    |        kind of        | \n| NAMES    | List users in a channel            |                                                |     no (planned)      |\n| LIST     | List channels on server            |                                                |     no (planned)      |\n| INVITE   | Invite user to channel             | Channel ops (if +i)                            |     no (planned)      |\n| WHO      | Query user info                    |                                                |     no (planned)      |\n| WHOIS    | Detailed user info                 |                                                |     no (planned)      |\n| WHOWAS   | Info on disconnected user          |                                                |     no (planned)      |\n| SUMMON   | Write to user's terminal           | If enabled                                     |     no (planned)      |\n| ISON     | Check if users are online          |                                                |     no (planned)      |\n| STATS    | Get server statistics              | Limited; Operators (full)                      | partial (planned yes) |\n| INFO     | Get server info                    |                                                | partial (planned yes) |       \n| TOPIC    | View or set channel topic          | Ops or anyone (set, depends on +t)             |          yes          |\n| TIME     | Get server time                    |                                                |          yes          |\n| ADMIN    | Get server admin info              |                                                |          yes          |\n| VERSION  | Get server version                 |                                                |          yes          |\n\n# flags\n\n## /modes\n\nnone of these are implemented through the chat postform, and instead are accessed through the netaris chat permissions menu.\n\n| Flag              | What it does                         | Who can set it      | Implemented in perms menu? |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------ | -----------