685	5t	# commands\n\n- here "kind of" means "the server implements it differently"\n    - `/ban`, `/unban`, and `/invite` are available to owner only, and take netaris username not irc nickname. it manages the "whitelist" or "blacklist" lists conditionally\n    - `/mode` is partially implemented to handle the permissions window. see more under section header FLAGS \n    - `/nick` is not callable from the text box. instead, display name is set in netaris settings\n    - `/join`, `/quit`, and `/kick` are not callable from the text box and instead are handled serverside \n\n| Command  | What it does                       | Who can use it                                 | impl. (netchats)      | impl. (IRC)           |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | :-------------------- | :-------------------- |\n| CONNECT  | Tell server to connect to another  | Operators                                      | no                    | yes (client)          |\n| SQUIT    | Disconnect a server link           | Operators                                      | no                    | no                    |\n| REHASH   | Reload server config               | Operators                                      | no                    | no                    |\n| WALLOPS  | Message to all operators           | Operators                                      | no                    | no                    |\n| OPERWALL | Alias for WALLOPS                  | Operators                                      | no                    | no                    |\n| RESTART  | Restart server                     | Operators                                      | no                    | no                    |\n| KILL     | Forcibly disconnect a user         | Operators                                      | no                    | no                    |\n| PASS     | Send password before registration  | On connect                                     | no                    | no                    |\n| USER     | Set username/realname on connect   | On connect                                     | no                    | no                    |\n| SERVER   | Server-to-server link registration | Servers only                                   | no                    | no                    |\n| OPER     | Authenticate as IRC operator       | With credentials                               | no                    | no                    |\n| PING     | Keepalive request                  | Usually server-initiated                       | no                    | yes (automatically)   |\n| PONG     | Keepalive response                 |                                                | no                    | yes (automatically)   |\n| TRACE    | Trace route to server              | Limited; Operators (full)                      | no                    | no                    |\n| LINKS    | List linked servers                |                                                | no                    | no                    |\n| ERROR    | Server error message               | Servers only                                   | no                    | no                    |\n| USERS    | List users on server host          | If enabled                                     | no                    | no                    |\n| AWAY     | Set away message                   |                                                | no                    | yes (client-server)   |\n| PRIVMSG  | Send message to user/channel       |                                                | no                    | yes (client-server)   |\n| USERHOST | Quick user host lookup             |                                                | no                    | yes (client-server)   |\n| NOTICE   | Like PRIVMSG but no auto-reply     |                                                | no                    | yes (client-server)   |\n| OP       | Give someone op status (+o)        | Channel ops                                    | no                    | no                    |\n| DEOP     | Remove someone's op status (-o)    | Channel ops                                    | no                    | no                    |\n| VOICE    | Give someone voice (+v)            | Channel ops                                    | no                    | no                    |\n| DEVOICE  | Remove someone's voice (-v)        | Channel ops                                    | no                    | no                    |\n| KICK     | Kick user from channel             | Channel ops                                    | no                    | no                    |\n| NAMES    | List users in a channel            |                                                | no (planned)          | yes (client-server)   |\n| LIST     | List channels on server            |                                                | no (planned)          | yes (client-server)   |\n| WHO      | Query user info                    |                                                | no (planned)          | no (planned)          |\n| WHOIS    | Detailed user info                 |                                                | no (planned)          | no (planned)          |\n| WHOWAS   | Info on disconnected user          |                                                | no (planned)          | no (planned)          |\n| SUMMON   | Write to user's terminal           | If enabled                                     | no (planned)          | no (planned)          |\n| ISON     | Check if users are online          |                                                | no (planned)          | yes (client-server)   |\n| QUIT     | Disconnect from server             |                                                | yes (not for client)  | yes                   |\n| JOIN     | Join a channel                     |                                                | yes (not for client)  | yes                   |\n| PART     | Leave a channel                    |                                                | yes (not for client)  | yes                   |\n| NICK     | Set or change nickname             |                                                | yes (not for client)  | no                    |\n| INVITE   | Invite user to channel             | Channel ops (if +i)                            | yes (owner)           | no                    |\n| MODE     | Set user or channel modes          | Self (user modes), Channel ops (channel modes) | yes (owner)           | no                    |\n| BAN      | Ban a user                         | Channel ops                                    | yes (owner)           | no                    |\n| UNBAN    | Remove a ban                       | Channel ops                                    | yes (owner)           | no                    |   \n| ME       | CTCP ACTION (/me waves)            |                                                | yes                   | yes                   |\n| TOPIC    | View or set channel topic          | Ops or anyone (set, depends on +t)             | yes                   | yes                   | \n| TIME     | Get server time                    |                                                | yes                   | yes                   |\n| ADMIN    | Get server admin info              |                                                | yes                   | yes                   |\n| VERSION  | Get server version                 |                                                | yes                   | yes                   |\n| STATS    | Get server statistics              | Limited; Operators (full)                      | partial (planned yes) | partial (planned yes) |\n| INFO     | Get server info                    |                                                | partial (planned yes) | partial (planned yes) | \n\n\n# flags\n\n## /mode\n\naccessed through the netaris chat permissions menu\n\n| Flag              | What it does                         | Who can set it      | Implemented in perms menu? |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| **Channel modes** |                                      |                     |                            |\n| +t                | Only ops can change topic            | Channel ops         | yes                        |\n| +s                | Secret (doesn't show in LIST)        | Channel ops         | yes                        |\n| +i                | Invite-only                          | Channel ops         | no (planned)               |\n| +m                | Moderated (only voiced/ops can talk) | Channel ops         | no (planned)               |\n| +k                | Requires password to join            | Channel ops         | no (planned)               |\n| +l                | User limit                           | Channel ops         | no (planned)               |\n| +o                | Give someone op status               | Channel ops         | no (planned)               |\n| +p                | Private                              | Channel ops         | no (not sure)              |\n| +v                | Give someone voice                   | Channel ops         | no (not sure)              |\n| +n                | No messages from outside channel     | Channel ops         | no (not planned)           |\n| +b                | Ban a mask                           | Channel ops         | no (not planned)           |\n| **User modes**    |                                      |                     |                            |\n| +i                | Invisible (don't show in WHO)        | Self only           | no (not planned)           |\n| +w                | Receive WALLOPS messages             | Self only           | "                          |\n| +s           