692	6a	\nyou can use whatever client you want. for demonstration, we are going to use weechat. to connect, run:\n\n```\n/server add netaris netar.is/6667\n/set irc.server.netaris.tls off\n/set irc.server.netaris.sasl_mechanism plain\n/set irc.server.netaris.sasl_username <username>\n/set irc.server.netaris.sasl_password <password>\n/connect netaris\n```\n\nfor most other clients, it's simpler. the requirements are:\n\n- server address: netar.is/6667 or netar.is:6667\n- login method: SASL (PLAIN)\n- username/Password: your credentials\n- disable SSL/TLS (or uncheck "Use SSL")\n\nweechat is particular in that it uses a slash instead of a colon to delineate the port. note that sending your password over sasl is secure. \n\n\n	2026-01-28 05:29:28.015+00	How to Connect to Netaris Chats via IRC Client	ca82df4d-b69e-4506-89bb-f86531d07d81
